---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const securitySchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "TechArticle",
  "headline": "IDSnap Security Architecture & On-Device Verification",
  "description": "Technical specifications of IDSnap's on-device cryptographic isolation, hardware KeyStore implementation, and the Airplane Mode verification test.",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "IDSnap Security Engineering",
    "url": "https://idsnap-bi3.pages.dev"
  }
};
---

<Layout
  title="Security Architecture & On-Device Cryptography | IDSnap"
  description="Technical specifications of IDSnap's on-device cryptographic isolation, hardware KeyStore implementation, and reproducible offline verification tests."
  schema={securitySchema}
>
  <div class="container legal-page-container">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Security Architecture' }]} />

    <div class="legal-header">
      <div class="badge-pill">
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
          <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/>
        </svg>
        Auditable Security Model
      </div>
      <h1 class="legal-title">Security Architecture & On-Device Proof</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Engineered for absolute privacy • Pure On-Device Execution</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Security Highlights Grid -->
    <h2 class="section-title" style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Core Cryptographic Pillars</h2>
    <div class="security-pillars-grid">
      <div class="card-glass pillar-card">
        <div class="pillar-icon"><svg class="icon-inline" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2" ry="2"></rect><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"></path></svg></div>
        <h3>Hardware KeyStore & Keychain</h3>
        <p>
          2FA TOTP secrets and vault keys are stored using Android KeyStore and iOS Keychain via hardware-backed cryptographic modules.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card-glass pillar-card">
        <div class="pillar-icon"><svg class="icon-inline" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M17.8 19.2 16 11l3.5-3.5C21 6 21.5 4 21 3c-1-.5-3 0-4.5 1.5L13 8 4.8 6.2c-.5-.1-.9.1-1.1.5l-.3.5c-.2.5-.1 1 .3 1.3L9 12l-2 3H4l-1 1 3 2 2 3 1-1v-3l3-2 3.5 5.3c.3.4.8.5 1.3.3l.5-.2c.4-.3.6-.7.5-1.2z"></path></svg></div>
        <h3>True Airplane Mode Operation</h3>
        <p>
          All engines (ML Kit OCR, PDFium, ID Card alignment, JPEG compressor) run locally. Document tools make no network calls; the only connections are made by Google's ad SDK (to show ads on a few screens) and, on Android, the one-time download of Google's document-scanner module.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card-glass pillar-card">
        <div class="pillar-icon"><svg class="icon-inline" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"></path></svg></div>
        <h3>App Switcher Shield (FLAG_SECURE)</h3>
        <p>
          Sensitive passport photos, bank scans, and 2FA codes are automatically obscured when switching apps in the recent-tasks carousel.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-body">
      <section id="airplane-mode" class="legal-section">
        <h2>1. The "Airplane Mode" Verification Test (Try It Yourself)</h2>
        <p>
          We believe privacy claims should be verifiable, not taken on faith. Anyone can verify that the tools work without a connection in 60 seconds:
        </p>
        <div class="test-steps-card">
          <h3>Reproducible Verification Protocol:</h3>
          <ol class="protocol-list">
            <li><strong>Enable Airplane Mode:</strong> Turn off all Wi-Fi, Cellular Data, and Bluetooth on your phone.</li>
            <li><strong>Launch IDSnap:</strong> The app opens normally and every feature works. (No ads are shown offline.)</li>
            <li><strong>Scan an ID Card:</strong> Take a photo of a front and back ID card. The edge detection and A4 layout generate immediately.</li>
            <li><strong>Extract Text (OCR):</strong> Run text extraction on any document. On-device Latin/Devanagari ML models process the text instantly.</li>
            <li><strong>Check 2FA Codes:</strong> Open the Authenticator tab. TOTP codes continue rolling every 30 seconds using the internal hardware clock.</li>
            <li><strong>Inspect Network Logs:</strong> Use Charles Proxy, Wireshark, or Android Network Profiler. While you scan, convert and use the authenticator you will see <strong>no document data transmitted</strong>; the only traffic is Google's ad SDK loading ads on the screens that show them.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="keychain" class="legal-section">
        <h2>2. Cryptographic Storage & Biometrics</h2>
        <p>
          IDSnap leverages the platform's native secure enclave for storing sensitive assets:
        </p>
        <div class="tech-spec-box">
          <div class="spec-row">
            <span class="spec-label">Android Storage:</span>
            <span class="spec-value">Android KeyStore Provider (AES-256 GCM encrypted SharedPreferences via <code>flutter_secure_storage</code>)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="spec-row">
            <span class="spec-label">iOS Storage:</span>
            <span class="spec-value">Apple Keychain Services (<code>kSecAttrAccessibleAfterFirstUnlockThisDeviceOnly</code>)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="spec-row">
            <span class="spec-label">Biometric Auth:</span>
            <span class="spec-value">Android <code>BiometricPrompt</code> & iOS <code>LocalAuthentication</code>. Biometric templates are never visible to app code.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="spec-row">
            <span class="spec-label">Database:</span>
            <span class="spec-value">Local Drift SQLite database located exclusively in the sandboxed app-private directory.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>3. Clipboard Safety Protocol</h2>
        <p>
          When you tap to copy a 6-digit 2FA code or an extracted text snippet, IDSnap flags the clipboard payload with the Android 13+ sensitive content flag (<code>EXTRA_IS_SENSITIVE</code>), preventing clipboard preview leakage. Furthermore, IDSnap automatically schedules a local clipboard purge 60 seconds after copying.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>4. Vulnerability Disclosure & Audit Reports</h2>
        <p>
          We welcome independent security researchers and privacy auditors. If you identify an issue or would like to submit a report:
        </p>
        <div class="contact-box">
          <p><strong>Security Team:</strong> <a href="mailto:security@idsnap.app">security@idsnap.app</a></p>
          <p><strong>PGP Key:</strong> Available upon email request.</p>
          <p><strong>Response SLA:</strong> We acknowledge security reports within 24 hours.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page-container {
    padding-top: 3.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
    max-width: 840px;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .legal-title {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .legal-meta {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--on-surface-variant);
  }

  .security-pillars-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }

  .pillar-card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .pillar-icon {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .pillar-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .pillar-card p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .legal-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  .legal-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--on-surface);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--outline-variant);
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .test-steps-card {
    background-color: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .test-steps-card h4 {
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--secondary);
  }

  .protocol-list {
    margin-left: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--on-surface-variant);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .tech-spec-box {
    background-color: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .spec-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }

  .spec-label {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .spec-value {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--on-surface);
  }

  .contact-box {
    background-color: var(--surface-container);
    border: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .security-pillars-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
